    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Two gaps, on purpose",
      "id": 13,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 47
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**There is no per-title history of what was deleted.** qbit-manage prints the torrent name and the verdict on separate lines, so no single log event carries both, and Prometheus holds state rather than events: `qbit_torrent_*` says what exists now and cannot say what existed last Tuesday. Closing that means one structured line per lifecycle event, emitted by a service that already reads the arrs, which Vector collects and VictoriaLogs indexes with no new plumbing at all.\n\n**And the freeleech lever moves in silence.** `tracker-control` runs every 30 minutes and decides three things: Radarr's freeleech-only filter, the Sonarr indexer, and autobrr's grab rate. Its log holds 92 lines and every one of them is a startup banner, so a decision that changes what gets grabbed leaves no trace. One line per change would put it on this page.\n\nWhat each site asks and what is configured against it lives on [Private trackers](/d/media-trackers/private-trackers). The path from announce to recycle bin is in [docs/lifecycle.md](https://github.com/PlatanosVerdes/rpi-homeserver/blob/main/docs/lifecycle.md)."
      }
    }
  ]
